  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Menton is an exception on the French Riviera: the town hall designates beaches specially set up for dogs. Hawaï beach, towards Garavan, is the one on this page. The tourist office describes it as a narrow beach east of the town, about 1 km from the Italian border, "probably the least crowded in Menton", lifeguarded in summer and close to the road, where you can also fish.</p>

      <h2>Good to know before you go</h2>
      <p>In its press release of 29 April 2026 ("Dogs on Menton's beaches: a reminder of the rules"), the town lists three beaches set up for dogs: Gorbio beach (on the Roquebrune-Cap-Martin border), Casino beach and Hawaï beach (Garavan). It announces a week of prevention by the municipal police aimed at dog owners, followed by fines for anyone breaking the rules. Its "Seafront and beaches" page only lists Hawaï and Casino as open to dogs and states that all other beaches are banned to animals, even on a leash. Its page on facilities for dog owners mentions three beaches "dedicated to dogs and their owners", marked with sails and signs.</p>
      <p>The Menton Riviera & Merveilles tourist office page (promenade Reine Astrid) states that dogs are allowed "on the right-hand side only" of Hawaï beach, which is open all year. The town hall does not repeat this restriction and, in the pages consulted, says nothing about leashes, dogs swimming, or any hours or seasonal period: to be safe, stay on the right-hand side of the beach, keep your dog on a leash and ask the town hall (04 92 10 50 00) if in doubt.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the Garavan area is very close to Italy — enough to walk in two countries on the same day.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Casino beach, more central, and Gorbio beach are the two other beaches the town hall lists for dogs. In town, the town hall lists two fenced, secure dog parks with drinking water (10 avenue Blasco Ibanez and 115 corniche Serres de la Madone) and bag dispensers, including eight in the Biovès gardens and at the Bastion. The Pointe des Douaniers beach in Cap-d'Ail is a few kilometres to the west.</p>
    </div>

